The viable family is Track B, not Track A. I’ll generate an affine/PGL-transformed multiplicative-subgroup block and ask for a normalized involutory \(PGL(2,p)\) stabilizer. Lemma 12 supplies the dihedral stabilizer and the planted certificate; generic stabilizer recovery enumerates images of three points, while the short route recovers the hidden translation from the finite-field barycenter and conjugates inversion. Seeds will vary the prime field so canonical PGL-equivalent blocks are not falsely counted as diverse.
