Built a native Track B generator based on the paper’s PGL block stabilizers from Lemma 12 and Theorem 13. It asks for an exact matrix witness preserving an affine subgroup block. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2408.14714v1)

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.14714/gen_2408_14714.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.14714/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.14714/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.14714/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.14714/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.14714/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five heuristic attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, averaging 300,724 modeled operations.
- Witness: 37 characters, four elements.
- Intended route: 135 exact operations.

The result is not yet eligible for submission: all 12 oracle calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” yielding zero scoreable attempts and no hardening verdict. The error transcripts are preserved honestly; no rejection or false hardness claim was recorded.
